'''Lomi Usqi Noodle Shop''' was a [[noodle]] [[restaurant]] owned by the [[alien]] barkeep [[Cabuck]].<ref name="Databank" />

{{Loc-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
Lomi Usqi Noodle Shop was introduced in "[[Lost / Found]]," the first episode of the [[2024]] television series ''[[Star Wars: The Acolyte]]''.<ref name="Episode I" /> The shop pays homage to the inn seen in the [[Wikipedia:Cinema of Hong Kong|Hong Kong]] [[Wikipedia:Shaw Brothers Studio|Shaw Brothers studio]] film [[Wikipedia:Come Drink with Me|''Come Drink with Me'']],<ref name="Trivia">{{SW|url=lost-found-trivia-gallery-the-acolyte|text="Lost / Found" Trivia Gallery &#124; The Acolyte}} {{C|Slide 1}}</ref> which was directed by [[Wikipedia:King Hu|King Hu]], set in the [[Wikipedia:Ming dynasty|Ming era]] (1368&mdash;1644), and released in [[1960s|1966]] under the [[Wikipedia:Traditional Chinese characters|Chinese]] title 大醉俠. Showrunner [[Leslye Headland]] stated that for ''The Acolyte'', she took inspiration from her favorite martial arts films, naming ''Come Drink with Me'' alongside the [[Wikipedia:Samurai cinema|Japanese samurai]] film [[Wikipedia:Yojimbo|''Yojimbo'']], directed by [[Wikipedia:Akira Kurosawa|Akira Kurosawa]] and released under the [[Wikipedia:Japanese language|Japanese]] title 用心棒 in 1961.<ref name="Headland trailer interview">{{SW|url=news/leslye-headland-interview|text="Whatever You Think ''The Acolyte'' Is, It's Not": ''Star Wars'' Series Creator Leslye Headland Revels in the First Teaser Trailer}}</ref>

